Z||000005||BroCar 87||09-11-2000||01:04 AM||||Think I got you guys beat.<BR>NACHO'S NACHO'S and more NACHO'S!!!!<BR>I am a manager at taco bell in a mall, and our food truck never came one day. So of course, we ran out of nacho's. I go to SAM'S WHOLESALE and purchase about $70.00 worth of Nacho chips and put them in my fiero. I pull up to the mall, pop the front truck, open the passenger door, and rear truck. I had 2 boxes of nacho's up front. A passenger compartment FULL of nacho bags (piled up onto the dash). Also I had the last couple boxes in the rear.<BR>You all should have seen everyone looking at my little car with all those nacho's!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000006||mrfiero||09-11-2000||01:05 AM||||I think I have you all beat!!<P>I have hauled a complete V-6 motor and 5-sp. Getrag tranny in the passenger compartment (seat removed).  It was a tight fit, but with the seat gone there's actually quite a bit of room.<P>I have also stuffed a GT front fascia, all 4 inner fender wells, and a bunch of misc. items in the passenger compartment (seat still there).<P>I used to haul all kinds of stuff on the outside when I owned a coupe.....doors, T-Top kits, etc.  It truly is my "truck"!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000007||Greg Piet||09-11-2000||01:15 AM||||Well I guess the weirdest thing I hauled was a set of 4 tires on a mini rack that connected to a class 2 hitch.  Yeah I know 4 tires big deal!   Well does the fact that the  rack had 2" of clearance to the ground, and I did that for over 2500 miles nonstop mean anything? ||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||09-11-2000||01:29 AM||||I guess I listed what I hauled IN my Fiero but here's what I've hauled WITH my Fiero:<P>I towed a Fiero from Denver to Maine, then (on the same trip) I hauled an other Fiero home from Detroit.<P>I'm about to drive to Oregon to pick up a car (non-Fiero) and haul it out east for a friend.  I'll be picking up an engine and a 5-sp., tranny along the way too!<P>Who ever said the Fiero wasn't versatile??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    ||||reg||10
Z||000009||Oreif||09-11-2000||01:34 AM||||OK A friend and I had 6 fishing poles inside Floor to rear window, The trunk had 2 tackle boxes, trolling motor, trolling battery, life vests, cooler, minnow bucket, and 2 jackets. We drove 3 hours to a lake fished all day (with a major storm passing thru in the afternoon) then drove to a motel then home. This was suppose to be a one day trip but we were too tired. It took us about 30 minutes to load the car in the rain after we were done fishing. Of course as soon as we loaded the car and got in it to start driving, the rain stopped and the sun came out!||||reg||1
