Z||000017||jlhuber||09-11-2000||07:53 AM||||i hauled an entire kx125 dirtbike (dissasembled of course) home from my uncle's house where it had just been repainted.  <BR>i have also hauled a whitetail deer home from the same uncle's house where i had just slammed into the deer at 55mph (that speed was after heavy braking).  oddly, it only caused $2500 worth of damage.  i thought it was going to be a lot worse.  thank god for full coverage insurance.<BR>i also brought home, and then the next day returned, a stereo that i bought from best buy.  it was big enough that i had to pull out the passenger seat and the t-tops, even then it would still barely fit.<BR>i hauled an air compressor home from a neighbor's house.  i stuck that in the trunk for i did not want to mess up my interior.<BR>those are about as wild as i have gotten... so far anyway ||||reg||1
