Z||000029||1FieroGTRacingInc||09-11-2000||11:04 PM||||Hey Everybody...<BR>I think I'm close to the best so far...<P>I'm a flooring tech. and my work truck was broke and I had a ceramic tile job to do that day....    Soooo..  lol..<BR>I loaded in the front compartment..<BR>8-50lbs. bag's of mortar<BR>4-25lbs. bag's of grout for the tile<BR>about 75lbs. of loose tool's(tile cutter,hammer's,etc..)<BR>in the Rear compartment i had<P>150 lbs. wet ceramic tile saw<BR>100 lbs. of misc.<P>AND INSIDE THE PASSENGER SEAT..<P>1,278 lbs. of ceramic tile... (that is what the weight said on the pallet that it was shipped on..)<BR> <BR>So I figured that i had around approx.   <P>          I was hauling around 2,105 lbs.<P><BR>   THE CAR WOULD'NT HARDLY TURN...  TAT GOD THAT I WAS ONLY GOING ABOUT 2 MILES....<P> HOW DO YA'LL LIKE THAT...   :d<BR>   Steve...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
